## Estructure Hook Service for (Use Modular):

Responsibility:

- Encapsulate stateful business logic, especially data fetching, processing, and side-effects.
- Keeps the Container component lean and easy to read.
- File naming: use-home-data.ts
- Location: /src/hooks/home/use-home-data.ts (or case not ref for screen /src/hooks/use-custom-hook.ts)

- Example: // /src/hooks/home/use-home-data.ts

```tsx
import { useState, useEffect } from "react";
import { homeService } from "./home-service";

export function useHomeData(userId: string) {
  const [levels, setLevels] = useState([]);
  const [progress, setProgress] = useState(null);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    async function fetchData() {
      setLoading(true);
      const levelsData = await homeService.getUserLevels(userId);
      const progressData = await homeService.getUserProgress(userId);
      setLevels(levelsData);
      setProgress(progressData);
      setLoading(false);
    }
    fetchData();
  }, [userId]);

  return { levels, progress, loading };
}
```

## Estructure Container for (Use Modular):

Responsibility:

- Handles business logic, orchestration, and state composition.
- Uses hooks to get data, process logic, handle callbacks, and passes everything as props to the Presenter (Screen).
- Never render UI directly (no JSX except calling the Presenter).
- File naming: home-container.tsx
- Location: /src/screens/home/home-container.tsx

- Example:

```tsx
import { HomeScreen } from '.../screens/home/home-screen';
import { useHomeData } from '.../hooks/home/use-home-data';

// App Router automatically passes params if needed
export default function Home() {
  const { levels, progress, loading } = useHomeData();

  return (
    <HomeScreen
      levels={levels}
      progress={progress}
      loading={loading}
      // Any other props/callbacks
    />
  );
```

## Estructure Presenter Screen for (Use Modular):

Responsibility:

- Purely presentational. Receives data and callback props, renders UI components, and handles user interaction callbacks.
- Should not fetch data or contain business logic.
- File naming: home-screen.tsx
- Location: /src/screens/home/home-screen.tsx

- Example:

```tsx
export function HomeScreen({ levels, progress, loading }: Props) {
  if (loading) return <ActivityIndicator />;
  return (
    <View>
      <Text>Nível atual: {progress?.currentLevel}</Text>
      {/* Render other UI with levels, etc */}
    </View>
  );
}
```

